     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "MATHENE · matheme-dia-syn-dia · ARGUED",
     "title": "Dia — The Cut",
     "italic": "The operator changed from a retained polar relation to a scalar result.",
     "body": "The bare relation is / = −/−. The carriers: (−1)+(+1)=0 cancels; (−1)−(+1)=−2 and (+1)−(−1)=+2 measure the whole span, orientation-dependent — the operator changed from retained polarity to scalar result. A zero sum forgets its summands; a difference of 2 forgets its endpoints: cancellation and appropriation, exactly demonstrable losses. A returned selection keeps input, criterion, result and the effects of exclusion.",
