     "italic": "A synchronic cut and a diachronic gathering are independent readings — neither classifies the other.",
     "body": "f(x) = x/2: state-space, rule and fixed point 0 form one configuration — every starting value converges. Histories differ: 8, 4, 2, 1, … and −4, −2, −1, … — the basin does not say which occurred. The crossing: a synchronic cut severs when the common condition is suppressed; a diachronic gathering severs when succession conceals its field. A schema is not automatically Syn; a narrative not automatically Dia.",
